From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Gui: take the batched paint engine's baked shaders from
 debian/painting-shaders

A quilt patch cannot carry the three baked shader files, and qtbase keeps
its .qsb files baked in the source because the baker is built from qtbase.
The source package carries them in debian/painting-shaders, listed in
debian/source/include-binaries, and the resource keeps the names the
engine asks for (QT_RESOURCE_ALIAS). Packaging only; a change offered to
Qt adds the files beside backingstorecompose.*.qsb instead.

Forwarded: not-needed
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2

--- a/src/gui/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/gui/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -348,9 +348,22 @@ qt_internal_add_resource(Gui "gui_shaders"
     FILES
         "painting/shaders/backingstorecompose.vert.qsb"
         "painting/shaders/backingstorecompose.frag.qsb"
-        "painting/shaders/batchpaint.vert.qsb"
-        "painting/shaders/batchpaint.frag.qsb"
-        "painting/shaders/batchpaint_dual.frag.qsb"
+)
+
+# The batched paint engine's baked shaders come from debian/painting-shaders (the source package
+# carries them there: a quilt patch cannot hold them); the resource keeps the names the engine asks for.
+set(batchpaint_shader_files)
+foreach(batchpaint_shader IN ITEMS batchpaint.vert.qsb batchpaint.frag.qsb batchpaint_dual.frag.qsb)
+    set(batchpaint_shader_file "${QtBase_SOURCE_DIR}/debian/painting-shaders/${batchpaint_shader}")
+    set_source_files_properties("${batchpaint_shader_file}"
+        PROPERTIES QT_RESOURCE_ALIAS "painting/shaders/${batchpaint_shader}")
+    list(APPEND batchpaint_shader_files "${batchpaint_shader_file}")
+endforeach()
+qt_internal_add_resource(Gui "gui_batchpaint_shaders"
+    PREFIX
+        "/qt-project.org/gui"
+    FILES
+        ${batchpaint_shader_files}
 )
 
 qt_internal_extend_target(Gui CONDITION QT_FEATURE_standarditemmodel
